     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Dear Fiona, thank you so much for your message about this and for diving into the code on GitHub. Yes, you are right – the models in compare_solution() are not correct. I double-checked (and checked what\r\n we wrote in the <a href=\"https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/articles/Introduction_to_tidyLPA.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/articles/Introduction_to_tidyLPA.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139428000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0dIVTx9svumpLTywNQ9SrP\">\r\nvignette here</a>!) and the change you suggested is correct. Note that we just made some changes to this function that introduced this issue—and (I think) this was working correctly previously. In fact, we used to have\r\n<b>tests </b>that benchmarked each function to known output, but in the coruse of making changes to the interface to the function we removed them. We’ll be sure to plan to add them back in future versions so this doesn’t happen again.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I just made the change in the development version and pushed the changes to GitHub; devtools::install_github(“jrosen48/tidyLPA”) should include this change.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Thank you so much for pointing this out.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Sincerely,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Josh<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:8.0pt;font-family:Times;color:black\">-- <br>\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:8.0pt\"><img border=\"0\" width=\"300\" height=\"65\" style=\"width:3.125in;min-height:.677in\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa/attach/a7abee96e8abb/image001.gif?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"http://images.utk.edu/images/interface/ut-emailsignature.gif\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:8.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:#58595b\"><a href=\"http://jmichaelrosenberg.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jmichaelrosenberg.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139428000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00BvZhNDStsHt8XShUP0yO\">Joshua M. Rosenberg, Ph.D.</a><u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:#58595b\">Assistant Professor, STEM Education<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:#58595b\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:#58595b\">Dept. of Theory and Practice in Teacher Education<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:#58595b\">The University of Tennessee, Knoxville<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:#58595b\">420 Claxton, 1122 Volunteer Boulevard, Knoxville, TN 37996<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:#58595b\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:#58595b\"><a href=\"tel:(865)%20974-5973\" value=\"+18659745973\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(865) 974-5973</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:Helvetica;color:#58595b\"><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jmros...@utk.edu</a></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">From: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Fiona Rupprecht &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fiona.s....@fau.de</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date: </b>Monday, October 29, 2018 at 6:01 AM<br>\r\n<b>To: </b>&quot;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a>&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject: </b>Update compare solutions<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear Dr. Baumeister, dear tidyLPA team, <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">concerning my e-mail from Friday I have now done some further calculations and also took a peek in the programming on Github.\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The first small issue I found is that the models are specified differently for the compare solutions command compared to the estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT command. Namely, the model with varying variances and zero covariances is specified\r\n as VVI in estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT, but as EEE in the compare solutions command. Similarly, the model with equal variances and equal covariances is specified as EEE in estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT, but as VVI in the compare solutions command.\r\n Assuming that the labeling in estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT is correct, this code should do it for the compare solutions command:\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>model &lt;- case_when(</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>variances == &quot;equal&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;zero&quot; ~ &quot;EEI&quot;,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>variances == &quot;varying&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;zero&quot; ~ &quot;<span style=\"color:red\">VVI</span>&quot;,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>variances == &quot;equal&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;equal&quot; ~ &quot;<span style=\"color:red\">EEE</span>&quot;,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span># variances == &quot;varying&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;equal&quot; ~ 4, # I&#39;d remove</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span># variances == &quot;equal&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;varying&quot; ~ 5,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>variances == &quot;varying&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;varying&quot; ~ &quot;VVV&quot;</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>)</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Apart from this, some further calculations have shown that the BIC and Log Likelihood values I get by working with estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT and specifying a equal-equal model are the same as the equal-zero model in the plot of\r\n the compare solutions command. Same way round, equal-zero values calculated with estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT are the same as equal-equal in the plot of the compare solutions command. However, I could not identify what one should change within the code.\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">For carrying on with my data analyses (which are unfortunately sort of urgent as they are part of a review) it would be completely enough for now to know which commands calculate “correctly”. So, are the estimate profiles and bootstrap\r\n LRT correct in specifying the models or is the compare solutions command correct?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks so much for your time and effort!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Fiona<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Fiona S. Rupprecht, MSc</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">PhD Student</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Institute for Psychogerontology</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">University of Erlangen-Nuremberg</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Kobergerstr. 62</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">90408 Nürnberg, Germany</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Fon 0049 911 5302-96112</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\"><a href=\"http://www.geronto.fau.de/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.geronto.fau.de/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139429000&amp;usg=AOvVaw14plFUT3wkLeSb21Sg5aSh\">http://www.geronto.fau.de/</a></span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;tidyLPA&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tidylpa+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139429000&amp;usg=AOvVaw15tiidPD7gVeBZYj4rBFOv\">https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tidylpa/26C29B4839130849BDF8FD4508137FA60F973217%40mbx1.exch.fau.de?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tidylpa/26C29B4839130849BDF8FD4508137FA60F973217%2540mbx1.exch.fau.de?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139429000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2g63VmFPnivLjVR4u-C_FT\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tidylpa/26C29B4839130849BDF8FD4508137FA60F973217%40mbx1.exch.fau.de</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139429000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0orPqghVJw6-WB2pFDGatB\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
