   "subject": "AW: Update compare solutions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"DE\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Dear Josh, <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I also thought that it might have happened in a recent change to the programming as I have worked with the package before.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Also, please know that there is no reproach or anything like this from my side. I think it is great that you have programmed it in the first place and that R and your Github page are\r\n transparent enough to retrace the programming and find a solution together. <u></u>\r\n<u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Sincerely, <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>Fiona<u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"DE\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b>Von:</b> Rosenberg, Joshua &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jmros...@utk.edu</a>&gt; <br>\r\n<b>Gesendet:</b> Montag, 29. Oktober 2018 18:51<br>\r\n<b>An:</b> Rupprecht, Fiona (IPG) &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fiona.s....@fau.de</a>&gt;; <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Betreff:</b> Re: Update compare solutions<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\">Dear Fiona, thank you so much for your message about this and for diving into the code on GitHub. Yes, you are right – the models in compare_solution() are not correct. I double-checked\r\n (and checked what we wrote in the <a href=\"https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/articles/Introduction_to_tidyLPA.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jrosen48.github.io/tidyLPA/articles/Introduction_to_tidyLPA.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139435000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1e30i-ujLrxMcuHoYBtDnf\">\r\nvignette here</a>!) and the change you suggested is correct. Note that we just made some changes to this function that introduced this issue—and (I think) this was working correctly previously. In fact, we used to have\r\n<b>tests </b>that benchmarked each function to known output, but in the coruse of making changes to the interface to the function we removed them. We’ll be sure to plan to add them back in future versions so this doesn’t happen again.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\">I just made the change in the development version and pushed the changes to GitHub; devtools::install_github(“jrosen48/tidyLPA”) should include this change.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\">Thank you so much for pointing this out.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\">Sincerely,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\">Josh<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:8.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times&quot;,serif;color:black\">-- <br>\r\n</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:8.0pt\"><img border=\"0\" width=\"300\" height=\"65\" style=\"width:3.125in;min-height:.6805in\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa/attach/aaa16bf3ccd56/image001.gif?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"http://images.utk.edu/images/interface/ut-emailsignature.gif\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:8.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:#58595b\"><a href=\"http://jmichaelrosenberg.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jmichaelrosenberg.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139435000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0BoxvHhCYPfcYeitW3XzEE\">Joshua M. Rosenberg, Ph.D.</a><u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:#58595b\">Assistant Professor, STEM Education<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:#58595b\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:#58595b\">Dept. of Theory and Practice in Teacher Education<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:#58595b\">The University of Tennessee, Knoxville<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:#58595b\">420 Claxton, 1122 Volunteer Boulevard, Knoxville, TN 37996<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:#58595b\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:#58595b\"><a href=\"tel:(865)%20974-5973\" value=\"+18659745973\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(865) 974-5973</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:9.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif;color:#58595b\"><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jmros...@utk.edu</a></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm 0cm 0cm\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">From:\r\n</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;color:black\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Fiona Rupprecht &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fiona.s....@fau.de</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Date: </b>Monday, October 29, 2018 at 6:01 AM<br>\r\n<b>To: </b>&quot;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a>&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject: </b>Update compare solutions<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Dear Dr. Baumeister, dear tidyLPA team, <u></u>\r\n<u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">concerning my e-mail from Friday I have now done some further calculations and also took a peek in the programming on Github.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">The first small issue I found is that the models are specified differently for the compare solutions command compared to the estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT command. Namely, the model with varying variances and zero\r\n covariances is specified as VVI in estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT, but as EEE in the compare solutions command. Similarly, the model with equal variances and equal covariances is specified as EEE in estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT, but as VVI in the\r\n compare solutions command. Assuming that the labeling in estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT is correct, this code should do it for the compare solutions command:\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">model &lt;- case_when(<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">variances == &quot;equal&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;zero&quot; ~ &quot;EEI&quot;,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">variances == &quot;varying&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;zero&quot; ~ &quot;<span style=\"color:red\">VVI</span>&quot;,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">variances == &quot;equal&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;equal&quot; ~ &quot;<span style=\"color:red\">EEE</span>&quot;,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"># variances == &quot;varying&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;equal&quot; ~ 4, # I&#39;d remove<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"># variances == &quot;equal&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;varying&quot; ~ 5,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"3\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">variances == &quot;varying&quot; &amp; covariances == &quot;varying&quot; ~ &quot;VVV&quot;<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:.75pt .75pt .75pt .75pt\"></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Apart from this, some further calculations have shown that the BIC and Log Likelihood values I get by working with estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT and specifying a equal-equal model are the same as the equal-zero\r\n model in the plot of the compare solutions command. Same way round, equal-zero values calculated with estimate profiles and bootstrap LRT are the same as equal-equal in the plot of the compare solutions command. However, I could not identify what one should\r\n change within the code. <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">For carrying on with my data analyses (which are unfortunately sort of urgent as they are part of a review) it would be completely enough for now to know which commands calculate “correctly”. So, are the estimate profiles\r\n and bootstrap LRT correct in specifying the models or is the compare solutions command correct?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Thanks so much for your time and effort!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Fiona<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Fiona S. Rupprecht, MSc</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">PhD Student</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Institute for Psychogerontology</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">University of Erlangen-Nuremberg</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Kobergerstr. 62</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">90408 Nürnberg, Germany</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Fon 0049 911 5302-96112</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt\"><a href=\"http://www.geronto.fau.de/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.geronto.fau.de/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139435000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Ew-jm6xzI_hcxKcenfJ8c\">http://www.geronto.fau.de/</a></span><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;tidyLPA&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tidylpa+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tid...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139435000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0aX5fYoWpj-guWdMVOgiL0\">https://groups.google.com/group/tidylpa</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tidylpa/26C29B4839130849BDF8FD4508137FA60F973217%40mbx1.exch.fau.de?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tidylpa/26C29B4839130849BDF8FD4508137FA60F973217%2540mbx1.exch.fau.de?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496139435000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2c_4Gnp1xB9xYDbJTBOpsD\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/